# Resident registration under attack, with the shipped policy (ALWAYS_ACTIVE: every capture answers challenges):
# a printed photo held still, an injected still stream (identical frames) and a video replay on a screen. Each
# attempt is refused with a generic message that does not say which check failed: "Face verification could not be
# completed" when passive PAD, integrity or binding rejects it, "We could not verify face liveness" when it reaches
# the challenges and cannot answer them. After the third the window shows the recovery guidance (the centre's
# supervisor process). The officer has no supervisor role, so no override is offered, and the registration is
# abandoned.
# The rigid-motion print (a-s2-print-affine) is in 60-config-sync.flow: the passive check alone accepts it (score
# 90, docs/eval/calibration-notes.md 3.2), and the shipped ALWAYS_ACTIVE policy refuses it there.
label registration 3: print, injected still stream and screen replay refused; maximum attempts, recovery guidance
set RESIDENT_NAME Chen Attacker
include lib/registration-start.flow
source a-s2-print-still
click #individualBiometricsScanBtn
expect (Face verification could not be completed|We could not verify face liveness) 60
snap attack-print-still
source a-s2-identical
click #retryButton
sleep 1500
expect (Face verification could not be completed|We could not verify face liveness) 60
snap attack-injected-still
source a-s2-screen-replay
click #retryButton
sleep 1500
expect after 3 attempts 60
snap attack-max-attempts
sql SELECT EVENT_ID, LOG_DESC FROM AUDIT.APP_AUDIT_LOG WHERE EVENT_ID IN ('REG-EVT-LV03','REG-EVT-LV06','REG-EVT-LV08','REG-EVT-LV09','REG-EVT-LV11') ORDER BY LOG_DTIMES DESC FETCH FIRST 8 ROWS ONLY
click #cancelButton
sleep 2000
click #homeImgView
sleep 1500
if-node #confirm click #confirm
sleep 2000
